1. `How to store significant bits of a number(in binary form) in a string` : first using `bitset<64>(n).to_string();`
    we converted our 64 binary digits of a number n and then using `variable f` we found first occurence of 1 and then
    we created a substr from `f ` till end . This works for any number greater than 0 . 
     string number = bitset<64>(n).to_string();
        size_t f = number.find('1');
        number = number.substr(f);
        
        
2.  `When we have to compare two big numbers raise to any big number ` : Comparing two numbers raise to some exponents. means 
    obviously this will even overflow our long long . So `A raise to B > C Raise to D` for this expression suppose we can 
    take log on both sides of equality because on a equality we can do equal things and after taking log we will get `B*log(A) > D*log(C)`
    and then we can easily put conditional operations and check because of log this will decrease our number in very
    minute and also make sure to use long double because log will return in decimal point and using integer type make
    give unintended output. And in below code we used long double inplace of double because precision of long double is
    better then double . 
     long double a,b,c,d;
    cin >> a >> b >> c >> d;
    if((double(b*log(a)))>double((d*log(c)))){
        cout << "YES" << '\n';
    }
    else{
        cout << "NO" << '\n';
    
    
3. `converting integer to string` : `int a; string s = to_string(a);` this will convert our integer a to string s.
